 \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/b9/b9364923447e278db5ec47bef74e1a05310645b30df22d4ea5efcc0de46c6ed2.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/16/16cb1608f70821d138f0c6984038bb42d86d9fbf76d560d94d2e25bd6fdb05e0.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/0a/0abbbaf34955fa40d6cdbfa9e16cb1567ee16271d65b4565206a0f2204eedf6d.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/4b/4b915439c3e9922d692aab4205a728160e0a1286f82fa5ebc736460901581147.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 false] [17592186059567 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](images/22/228e4520f4301ac7acb7eef54fad6dcc8ce9bbf43d48124a761978dfcea6423b.svg)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186059567 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](images/c9/c9b7abb2641034c1769c6fe6b13b96edd7ccc282b61424b2031a3d37faa456e4.png)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 false] [17592186059567 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/80/80100c3398fa2eac3a07696dd30354c3c971f0650ab32d67a958492ed1cbdeae.svg)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/8f/8f7fdfc0426ad23a34e6d7f2915181a88a63ea74da93b2b6bd718e03f21ba8d2.svg)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/28/2867d40f70d0e042e522e1bb14ea8af830e42f22a63cc482ba67923c51807312.svg)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/9a/9a4c39673ffd559b35ed9dbf0e465f6a8714c0d9a467178a51e1f6ad79a81445.svg)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186059567 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/6f/6f1bf319faf8be4a9a79c0a6f9301e6eac48a5b04f66949b679e8445b07e9d9c.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/fc/fc1ac06787ed64ebefbb1a7a82f9bf785525777f61831bbbc39bd25c7e629d5a.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/d0/d0249dcecf6b75cd6ff7c4623beac6fd6cfae64a58d043bb6759440167f40ea1.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/64/64d1f57717dda57c8a7fbc403728ee9699a22ce995f68a50a0b80f25543fdab6.png)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 false] [17592186059757 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426755 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186059757 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426758 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186059758 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426756 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186059758 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426757 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186059888 1050 420.0 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186060276 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y+z=2 \\\\ x-6y+11z=3 \\\\ 3x-4y-z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & a \\\\ 1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186060276 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y+z=2 \\\\ x-6y+11z=3 \\\\ 3x-4y-z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & a \\\\ 1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 false] [17592186060935 1064 "Remember that we can represent a system of two linear equations in two variables using matrices. We can do the same thing for a system of three linear equations in three variables, such as the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y\\text{ }-\\text{ }2z=7 \\\\ 2x\\text{ }-\\text{ }1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }4z=2 \\\\ 2x+1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a $3 \\times 3$ system like the one above, we put the coefficients of the system into a $3 \\times 3$ coefficient matrix:\n\n![](images/40/40541d2ecb10c763056ae72734e723a9d5967ed9accaf0bbde6f2a2f9ec96b65.svg)\n\nEach row has the coefficients of one of the equations in the system, and each column consists of the coefficients of one particular variable.\nWe also have the $3 \\times 1$ column vectors\n\n![](images/e5/e56ed72d2d17f9a4bc59bfe51a96534a72ebe481a312b8e9c6c028ade96d3748.svg)\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{b}$ consists of each constant on the right side of the system and $\\mathbf{x}$ contains the variables.\nWith these matrices, we can write our system as $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ or\n\n![](images/f0/f06e5a54e106bcdca8b5cbad677ade3476ba8f6218b4aa79d196f54e0fff3e2c.svg)\n\nWe can write any system of three equations with three variables in this form. Just to check that the above equation is true, let's multiply out the left-hand side to see if it equals the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3x+2y\\text{ }-\\text{ }2z \\\\ 2x\\text{ }-\\text{ }1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }4z \\\\ 2x+1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }3z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =b\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186060935 1064 "Remember that we can represent a system of two linear equations in two variables using matrices. We can do the same thing for a system of three linear equations in three variables, such as the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y\\text{ }-\\text{ }2z=7 \\\\ 2x\\text{ }-\\text{ }1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }4z=2 \\\\ 2x+1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a $3 \\times 3$ system like the one above, we put the coefficients of the system into a $3 \\times 3$ coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nEach row has the coefficients of one of the equations in the system, and each column consists of the coefficients of one particular variable.\nWe also have the $3 \\times 1$ column vectors\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{b}$ consists of each constant on the right side of the system and $\\mathbf{x}$ contains the variables.\nWith these matrices, we can write our system as $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ or\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe can write any system of three equations with three variables in this form. Just to check that the above equation is true, let's multiply out the left-hand side to see if it equals the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3x+2y\\text{ }-\\text{ }2z \\\\ 2x\\text{ }-\\text{ }1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }4z \\\\ 2x+1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }3z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =b\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 false] [17592186265930 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ -6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186265930 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ -6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 false] [17592186265930 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5.$" 13194139534588 17592186045417 true] [17592186265930 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nN